course: dictionary
lesson: 13410
title: Hibernating: a long winter rest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hibernating means spending the winter in a deep, sleep-like rest. Some animals do not just nap for one night. They can rest for weeks or months. «The hedgehog is hibernating under the leaves all winter.» The clues are winter and all winter: this rest happens in the cold months.
explain: Look at the word's parts: hibernate, then -ing. The -ing ending can show something happening right now, as in «The bats are hibernating in the cave.» It can also describe an animal, as in «a hibernating animal», meaning an animal that is in this long winter rest.
explain: A hibernating animal's body slows right down. Its heartbeat and breathing slow, and its body temperature drops. It lives on fat it stored up before winter. «Before we lit the bonfire, we checked the leaf pile for hibernating animals.» Because they are resting, we must leave them alone.
fact: Hibernating means spending the winter in a deep, sleep-like rest.
fact: «Hibernating» can describe what an animal is doing, or describe the animal itself: a hibernating hedgehog.
fact: Animals that hibernate include hedgehogs, bats, dormice, some bears, and many frogs and snakes.
fact: When an animal hibernates, its heartbeat and breathing slow down, and it lives on stored fat.
fact: The phrases «go into hibernation» and «wake from hibernation» use the noun hibernation, which means the long winter rest itself.
exercise: «The hedgehog is hibernating under the leaves all winter.» When is the hedgehog resting? | In the summer, while it plays | *All winter | Only at night | During lunchtime
exercise: «Before the bonfire, we checked the leaf pile for hibernating animals.» Why did they check the leaf pile? | *Because the animals are resting and could be hurt | To count how many leaves there are | To find a good place for a picnic | To feed the animals before the fire
exercise: Which animal hibernates? | A goat climbing a steep hill | *A dormouse that sleeps through the cold months | A kitten chasing a ball all day | A lion hunting on the plains
test: «The bear woke from hibernation when spring came.» When did the bear's winter rest end? | *When spring came | When winter began | Every night at midnight | In the middle of summer
test: Which phrase describes an animal that is in its long winter rest? | *A hibernating animal | A singing bird | A swimming fish | A running dog
exam: «Bats spend the cold months hibernating in caves.» What does hibernating mean here? | *Spending the winter in a deep, sleep-like rest | Hunting for food all night | Playing loudly in the dark | Flying south to warmer places
